{
 "_doc": "S6-B3221 reviewed register for scripts/context_bullets_census.py - DATA, not code (CSV-first; the output_audit/preleg_lifecycle_exemptions.json precedent). Each group names bullet numbers a reader compared against the gate AND the producer and found true, keyed [strategy, side, bullet index, token], with the reason. An anchor is a producer line the number comes from, with the count of its occurrences: if the producer changes the line, the count moves and the census check fails until the bullet is re-read - so producer-constant drift is caught too. A group with no anchor is a label, a form name, a literature figure or a quoted measurement. 'retired' lists the 80 bullet texts S6-B3221 corrected or removed on 69 sides, in the census's rendering (an f-string's values shown as {...}); the check fails if one comes back on its side. 'statuses' lists the declaration sides the census cannot read as a literal bullet list - [strategy, side, status, reason], counted as a multiset - and --check fails on any other non-OK side, on an entry no side matches, and on an entry with a blank reason (S6-B3276).",
